=== 3. the same race won by hand, before the drop-in existed: a manual `systemctl start` at t=1340 ===
  [ 1340.364414] systemd: Starting repowerd.service
  [ 1340.402335] repowerd[1006137]: main: Starting repowerd 2025.09
  [ 1340.587955] systemd: Started repowerd.service       <- 0.19 s, no stall, no timeout, no SEGV
  [ 1340.6885xx] repowerd: Falling back to NullHBM / NullPerformanceBooster   <- benign, same in both runs
  and it stayed up: `systemctl is-active repowerd` = active, com.lomiri.Repowerd on the system bus.
  Difference from the failed boot: sensorfwd had already been READY for ~1250 s.
  (It was 1296.086085 that the first manual attempt started; that one is not in this log because the
   boot journal's early lines had already been rotated past. The 1340 one is the one on record.)

=== 4. the drop-in that fixes it (installed at /etc/systemd/system/repowerd.service.d/) ===
  [Unit]
  After=sensorfwd.service
  Wants=sensorfwd.service
  
  [Service]
  Restart=on-failure
  RestartSec=5

=== 5. the live proof: stop both, ask for repowerd alone, watch the jobs ===
    systemctl stop repowerd; systemctl stop sensorfwd
    systemctl start repowerd &
    t=1  jobs: 23234 sensorfwd.service start running | 23105 repowerd.service start waiting

=== 6. that run's journal: ordering honoured, load_plugin succeeded, no SEGV ===
  [ 1739.394428] sensorfw: Hybris sensor manager initialized
  [ 1739.422482] systemd: Started sensorfwd.service
  [ 1739.445080] systemd: Starting repowerd.service          <- 23 ms after sensorfwd's READY
  [ 1739.460103] sensorfw: minLimit: 0 0                     <- the load_plugin success signature
  [ 1739.460667] sensorfw: maxLimit: 2147483647 2147483647
  [ 1739.487316] repowerd: main: Starting repowerd 2025.09
  [ 1739.857200] systemd: Started repowerd.service           <- no 10 s stall, no timeout

  the load_plugin signature appears exactly twice in the whole boot: t=112 (after the shell
  had already given up) and t=1739 (this run). Once per successful load_plugin, never per attempt.

